hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22231","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Habib al-Ansari, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Bashir and the daughter of Abi Bashir narrating from their father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said about fever: Cool it with water, for it is from the blast of Hell."
"22232","Rawh and Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, that Abu Bashir al-Ansari informed him that he was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in some of his journeys, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a messenger: No necklace of string shall remain on the neck of a camel, nor any necklace, except it is cut. Ismail said: I think he said: While the people were in their fasting."
"22233","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, Habban ibn Wasi narrated to me, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Zayd and Abi Bashir al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them one day, and a woman passed at al-Batha, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, signaled to her to hold back, so she went back until he prayed, then she passed."
"22234","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah said, and I heard it from Harun, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, Makhrama informed me, from his father, from Said ibn Nafi, he said: Abu Bashir al-Ansari, the companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw me praying the Duha prayer when the sun had risen, so he criticized me for that and forbade me, then said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not pray until the sun rises high, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."
